<Document lang="en" page="support" title="Support" description="Learn how to start a comparison, save your progress, and report a problem.">
  <section>
    <h2>Start a comparison</h2>
    <p>zcompare is designed for macOS 15 Sequoia and later. In a new comparison window, select or drag in two files or two folders, then start the comparison. The app detects the comparison mode from your inputs.</p>
    <p>To see the interface first, try the <a href="/en#compare">text, image, and binary comparison examples</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Save progress or share results</h2>
    <p>Save a comparison session to resume your review later. To share the results, export an HTML or JSON report and check whether it includes source content, thumbnails, or file names before sending it.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Report a problem</h2>
    <p>Search for an existing issue or submit feedback on <a href="https://github.com/zwyyy456/zcompare/issues">GitHub Issues</a>. Include your zcompare version, macOS version, comparison mode, steps to reproduce, and what happened. If you attach samples or screenshots, remove private paths, file contents, and credentials.</p>
  </section>
</Document>
